SUMMARY:Jessie Maple Patton Day in Bloomington\, Indiana
DESCRIPTION:Will (Jessie Maple\, 1981) is the one of the earliest survivi
 ng features directed by a Black American woman. The Black Film Center &am
 p\; Archive has been a proud steward of the film elements\, and much more
 \, since the acquisition of The Jessie Maple Collection (https://indiana.
 us17.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&amp\;id=d44e
 e48512&amp\;e=9b80f7f3db) in 2005. Having undergone a 4K restoration\, Wi
 ll is screening for audiences around the world!&#160\;Now\, Jessie Maple'
 s films are also available to watch from the comfort of your own home on 
 Criterion Channel! Will is included as part of the Black Debutantes (http
 s://indiana.us17.list-manage.com/track/click?u=f603b0d14ab6059bea01fbc72&
 amp\;id=2d70d816f1&amp\;e=9b80f7f3db) lineup\, which is a "celebration of
  pioneering Black women who made an impact with their very first—and in
  some cases only—feature film." Twice is Nice (Jessie Maple\, 1989) is 
 also available.  To research the Jessie Maple collection\, please send an
  email to bfca@iu.edu (mailto:bfca@iu.edu).
